# Aether for WebCLAP

Aether by sletz, a hybrid polyphonic synthesizer written in Faust (subtractive, four-operator FM and additive
engines, a modulation matrix, a 16-step sequencer and a stereo effects bus), ported to WebCLAP. This is not an
official faust-aether release.

- faust-aether: https://github.com/sletz/faust-aether (commit 28f262c1de87ae9fae424be7ee22bcbf665cd7bd)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-faust-aether.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here and
  runs the pinned Faust compiler (2.88.0) on upstream's `aether.dsp` / `effects.dsp` (`ports/faust-aether/gen.py`).

